messages:
elaine: Quick review request for PR 1488 1 compact guide that ties together function/tool calling examples, a tiny JSON schema, and a recommended parse-fallback. Looking for: clarity, SDK parity (py/js), and link sanity.

matt: I'll scan it now. Does the PR use the new field names? (invocations vs tools)

elaine: Yes, examples updated to invocations. The schema uses nullable meta to avoid forcing callers into defensive null checks.

sam: Can you drop the schema here? I'll validate against our internal lint.

elaine: Schema snippet in the PR:

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "command": {"type": "string"},
    "args": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}},
    "meta": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object"}, {"type": "null"}]},
    "status": {"type": "string", "enum": ["ok","error"]}
  },
  "required": ["command","status"]
}

nina: Looks good. Suggest a short note in the prose: "runtime may add transient keys; prefer tolerant parsing." Keeps the sample readable without changing schema.

matt: Also recommend a tiny JS helper to normalize meta so users copy fewer guards.

elaine: Added this helper to the JS snippet: function normalizeMeta(obj){ return obj.meta ?? {}; }
const output = response.invocations?.[0]?.output || {};
const meta = normalizeMeta(output);

sam: For Python use safe gets: inv = response.get("invocations", []); out = inv[0].get("output", {}) if inv else {}

elaine: Added a two-line py example and a 3-line fallback pseudo-code for non-JSON responses: try: parsed = json.loads(text) except ValueError: parsed = fallback_regex(text)

lily-bot: link-check: found one deprecated internal doc link in the runbook reference.

nina: I'll patch the broken link and re-run.

matt: +1 after link fix and minor wording tweak.
sam: +1 for schema and snippets.

elaine: Thanks everyone 1 will merge after the link patch and then post a changelog entry with links to the SDK snippet sandbox.
